<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/13th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Conquest of Wales by Edward I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1277–1283</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wales">Wales</a> by Edward I was the series of English campaigns of 1277 and 1282–1283 that ended the independent Welsh principality ruled from Gwynedd. After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/llywelyn-ap-gruffudd">Llywelyn ap Gruffudd</a> was killed in December 1282 and his brother Dafydd captured, Edward annexed the principality, imposed English administration through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/statute-of-rhuddlan">Statute of Rhuddlan</a> (1284) and built castles such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caernarfon">Caernarfon</a>, Conwy and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harlech">Harlech</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/conquest-of-wales-by-edward-i.jpg" alt="Conquest of Wales by Edward I" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Edward_I_-_Westminster_Abbey_Sedilia.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
